13:["$","p","p-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Level:"}]," Intermediate → Advanced",["$","br","br-0",{}],"\n",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"Project Type:"}]," Practical DevOps / Cloud Automation Portfolio",["$","br","br-1",{}],"\n",["$","strong","strong-2",{"children":"Main Stack:"}]," Terraform + AWS + Ansible + Git + GitHub Actions"]}]
14:["$","blockquote","blockquote-0",{"children":["\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":["🟦 ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Project goal:"}]," Define cloud infrastructure with Terraform, configure Linux servers with Ansible, validate changes through CI, and document how to verify, operate, and safely clean up the environment."]}],"\n"]}]
15:["$","hr","hr-0",{}]
16:["$","h1","h1-1",{"children":"🧭 1. Project Overview"}]
17:["$","p","p-3",{"children":"In this project, you will learn to automate two different layers of infrastructure work:"}]
18:["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Terraform"}]," creates and manages cloud resources such as a VPC, subnets, security groups, and EC2 instances."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Ansible"}]," configures operating-system-level settings and software on reachable Linux hosts."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Git"}]," stores the source code and records changes."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"GitHub Actions"}]," can run formatting, syntax, and static validation checks before code is merged."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"AWS IAM"}]," controls which identities can perform cloud actions."]}],"\n"]}]
19:["$","p","p-4",{"children":"The project starts with code review and validation. Creating AWS resources is a separate, intentional step that can incur charges. You can inspect and validate much of the repository without connecting to AWS."}]
1a:["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"🎯 Learning outcomes"}]
1b:["$","p","p-5",{"children":"By the end, you should be able to explain:"}]
1c:["$","ol","ol-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"What Infrastructure as Code (IaC) means and why teams use it."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"The difference between Terraform provisioning and Ansible configuration management."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"How VPCs, public/private subnets, route tables, and security groups fit together."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"How Terraform state works and why it must be protected."}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"How an Ansible inventory connects playbooks to hosts."}],"\n",["$","li","li-5",{"children":"How to validate changes before applying them."}],"\n",["$","li","li-6",{"children":"How to reduce accidental exposure and cloud costs."}],"\n",["$","li","li-7",{"children":"How to troubleshoot common Terraform, AWS, SSH, and Ansible failures."}],"\n"]}]
1d:["$","hr","hr-1",{}]
1e:["$","h1","h1-2",{"children":"🏢 2. Real-Time Business Scenario"}]
1f:["$","p","p-6",{"children":["Imagine a company named ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"CloudKart"}]," needs a small Linux application environment in AWS."]}]
20:["$","p","p-7",{"children":"The team wants a repeatable process. A new environment should not depend on someone manually clicking through the AWS Console and remembering every setting."}]
21:["$","h3","h3-1",{"children":"❌ Manual approach"}]
22:["$","ul","ul-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"An engineer creates a VPC by clicking through the console."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Another engineer creates a security group with slightly different rules."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Server setup commands are copied and pasted manually."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Documentation gets out of date."}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"Rebuilding the environment after a failure takes too long."}],"\n"]}]
23:["$","h3","h3-2",{"children":"✅ Automated approach"}]
24:["$","ol","ol-1",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Engineers update Terraform files in Git."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"CI checks formatting and validates the configuration."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"An authorized engineer reviews the plan."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Terraform provisions the approved AWS resources."}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"Ansible configures the reachable Linux host."}],"\n",["$","li","li-5",{"children":"The engineer verifies the result and records the evidence."}],"\n",["$","li","li-6",{"children":"Changes are reviewed, versioned, and repeatable."}],"\n"]}]
25:["$","blockquote","blockquote-1",{"children":["\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":["🟨 ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Important distinction:"}]," Terraform is mainly responsible for provisioning infrastructure. Ansible is mainly responsible for configuring systems and applications on that infrastructure. They complement each other; they are not interchangeable tools."]}],"\n"]}]
26:["$","hr","hr-2",{}]
27:["$","h1","h1-3",{"children":"🎨 3. Architecture — Colourful Diagrams"}]
28:["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"3.1 End-to-end architecture"}]
29:["$","pre","pre-0",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-mermaid","children":"flowchart TD\r\n    DEV[\"👩‍💻 DevOps Engineer\"] --> GIT[\"📦 Git Repository\"]\r\n    GIT --> PR[\"🔍 Pull Request / Code Review\"]\r\n    PR --> CI[\"⚙️ GitHub Actions Validation\"]\r\n    CI --> FMT[\"Terraform fmt + validate\"]\r\n    CI --> LINT[\"Ansible syntax / lint checks\"]\r\n    FMT --> APPROVE[\"✅ Review Plan and Approve\"]\r\n    LINT --> APPROVE\r\n    APPROVE --> TF[\"🏗️ Terraform\"]\r\n    TF --> AWS[\"☁️ AWS Account\"]\r\n    AWS --> VPC[\"🌐 VPC and Subnets\"]\r\n    AWS --> SG[\"🛡️ Security Groups\"]\r\n    AWS --> EC2[\"🖥️ EC2 Linux Instance\"]\r\n    EC2 --> ANS[\"🔧 Ansible over SSH\"]\r\n    ANS --> PKG[\"📦 Packages and Configuration\"]\r\n    PKG --> VERIFY[\"🧪 Service and Security Verification\"]\r\n    VERIFY --> DOC[\"📸 Evidence + Documentation\"]\n"}]}]
2a:["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"3.2 Terraform vs Ansible — responsibility boundary"}]
2b:["$","pre","pre-1",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-mermaid","children":"flowchart LR\r\n    subgraph TERRAFORM[\"🟪 Terraform — Provisioning\"]\r\n        T1[\"VPC\"]\r\n        T2[\"Subnet\"]\r\n        T3[\"Security Group\"]\r\n        T4[\"EC2 Instance\"]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph ANSIBLE[\"🟥 Ansible — Configuration\"]\r\n        A1[\"Connect over SSH\"]\r\n        A2[\"Install Packages\"]\r\n        A3[\"Manage Configuration\"]\r\n        A4[\"Start / Enable Service\"]\r\n    end\r\n    T4 --> A1 --> A2 --> A3 --> A4\n"}]}]
2c:["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"3.3 Change lifecycle"}]
2d:["$","pre","pre-2",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-text","children":"📝 Edit code\r\n    ↓\r\n🔍 Format and validate\r\n    ↓\r\n👀 Review Terraform plan\r\n    ↓\r\n✅ Approve intended change\r\n    ↓\r\n☁️ Terraform apply (only when authorized)\r\n    ↓\r\n🖥️ Confirm host is reachable\r\n    ↓\r\n🔧 Run Ansible playbook\r\n    ↓\r\n🧪 Verify service, ports, logs, and permissions\r\n    ↓\r\n📚 Save evidence and update README\n"}]}]
2e:["$","h3","h3-3",{"children":"📦 Diagram legend"}]
